    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хотя...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Если ты ему жизнь спасёшь...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Может, он нас и простит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Стульчик, да?",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the exchange around Can I help line by line and unpack how the Russian works.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф, может помочь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, can I help?' There is no question word here — in Russian, rising intonation on 'to help' is enough to make it a question. And Chef jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Не знаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I don't know.' The negative particle sits directly before the verb for 'know' to negate the action.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Меня он оштрафовал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He fined me.' Chef Barinov delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'to fine'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Тебя депортировать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You must be deported.' Chef Barinov delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'deport'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Думаю, что это?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I'm thinking, what is this?' Chef Barinov delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'I think'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Думаю, нет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I don't think so.' Chef Barinov delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'I think'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "С другим может...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maybe with another...' Chef Barinov delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'can'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Договориться удастся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We could negotiate.' Chef Barinov uses the perfective verb meaning 'to agree' to focus on the single completed result, pairing it with 'to succeed'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вот.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'There.' Ainura delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'there'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хотя...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Though...' Ainura delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'at least'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Если ты ему жизнь спасёшь...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'If you save his life...' The phrasing opens with 'life' before bringing in 'to save' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Может, он нас и простит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maybe he will forgive us.' Ainura chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'can' for the ongoing action, followed by 'will forgive'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Стульчик, да?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'A chair, right?' Ainura turns a statement into a question purely through rising intonation on the word meaning 'little chair' to make the point directly in conversation. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
